    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Disaster_Response_Logistics\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    depots = list(range(2))  # D0..D1\n    units = list(range(3))  # U0..U2\n    supplies = list(range(2))  # S0..S1\n    days = list(range(2))  # Day0..Day1\n\n    demands = [[[11.16, 43.9], [36.32, 16.49]], [[41.52, 12.66], [13.6, 29.05]], [[40.4, 39.2], [26.61, 14.38]]]\n    depot_supplies = [[[37.44, 55.65], [49.07, 26.99]], [[57.31, 43.57], [49.5, 44.74]]]\n    transport_costs = [[1.28, 3.37, 4.75], [3.06, 3.31, 4.95]]\n    risk_costs = [[132.54, 195.62, 190.13], [134.33, 174.98, 122.62]]\n    supply_volumes = [1.92, 1.66]\n    penalty_costs = [56.76, 79.83]\n    vehicle_cost = 10.0\n    vehicle_capacity = 100.0\n    total_vehicles = 20\n\n    # Decision variables\n    # Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Amount of supply s from depot d to unit u on day t\n    flows = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                for s in supplies:\n                    flows[(d, u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Shortage of supply s at unit u on day t\n    slacks = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                slacks[(u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Number of vehicles on route d->u on day t\n    vehicles = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                vehicles[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.INTEGER, name=f\"Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Route d->u is active on day t (binary)\n    routes = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                routes[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total cost (transport + penalty + vehicle + risk)\n    obj = quicksum(\n        transport_costs[d][u] * flows[(d, u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        penalty_costs[s] * slacks[(u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        vehicle_cost * vehicles[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        risk_costs[d][u] * routes[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Depot capacity constraints: Total outflow <= supply\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for u in units) <= depot_supplies[d][s][t],\n                    name=f\"DepotCap_D{d}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Inflow + slack >= demand\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for d in depots) + slacks[(u, s, t)] >= demands[u][s][t],\n                    name=f\"Demand_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Vehicle capacity constraints: Total volume <= vehicles * capacity\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(supply_volumes[s] * flows[(d, u, s, t)] for s in supplies) <= vehicle_capacity * vehicles[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"VehCap_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Route activation constraints: vehicles <= total_vehicles * route\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    vehicles[(d, u, t)] <= total_vehicles * routes[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"RouteAct_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Fleet size constraints: Total vehicles <= total_vehicles\n    for t in days:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(vehicles[(d, u, t)] for d in depots for u in units) <= total_vehicles,\n            name=f\"FleetSize_Day{t}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Situation:\nA severe storm system has caused flooding and landslides across the operational area. Primary distribution will originate from Supply Depot Alpha (adjacent to the airfield) and Supply Depot Bravo (near the port). Receiving sites include Field Hospital Echo, Community Shelter Delta, and the Riverside Distribution Point. Key ground lines of communication are degraded; river crossings are weight-restricted and mountain passes are intermittently closed for debris clearance. Offload windows at the receiving sites are limited by curfew and available handling teams. Fuel and driver availability are constrained. Routes through the valley are exposed to hazardous conditions and require coordinated security escorts and engineer route clearance.\n\nMission:\nDeliver life-sustaining commodities to designated receiving sites over the current operational period while minimizing total operational cost, defined as the sum of transport costs, shortage penalties, per-vehicle deployment costs, and fixed route security risk costs. Prioritize medical support and potable water resupply while maintaining safety of movement and preserving fleet integrity.\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Supply and demand: Each depot\u2019s outbound throughput is limited by daily available stocks and handling capacity; each receiving site has specified daily requirements by commodity. Controlled shortfalls are permissible only under penalty when access or supply is constrained, and will be used as a last resort to maintain feasibility.\n- Routing and activation: Movements are planned by origin\u2013destination, commodity, and day. Vehicles may only be assigned to routes that are activated for that day. Activating any route (sending one or more vehicles) incurs a fixed Risk Cost representing security overhead (escort teams, route clearance), independent of the number of vehicles dispatched on that route that day. Consolidate shipments to reduce repeated activations where feasible without exceeding offload limits.\n- Vehicles and loads: Each vehicle carries a cost to deploy and has a fixed carrying capacity. Commodities have different stowage densities; load planning must respect vehicle capacity by commodity volume. Total vehicles dispatched per day cannot exceed fleet availability. Weight-restricted bridges and soft shoulders constrain heavy loads; use lighter vehicles on vulnerable segments if required.\n- Transport costs: Route-specific transport costs reflect distance, road condition, and backhaul limitations. Favor closer or safer corridors when cost-effective, but account for site access windows and the need to avoid splitting critical items across multiple days if it jeopardizes clinical operations.\n- Risk and safety: Security posture changes may close or degrade routes without notice. Avoid activating high-risk corridors for marginal loads. Coordinate with security and engineer elements to schedule route openings and clearance windows aligned with convoy departures.\n- Coordination measures: Stagger departures from Depots Alpha and Bravo to deconflict choke points and synchronize with receiving site offload teams. Issue daily movement orders detailing activated routes, convoy compositions, and contingency reroutes. Maintain communication checks at key terrain to trigger go/no-go decisions if conditions deteriorate.\n- Outcome: The dispatch plan will determine, by day, which depots supply which sites, the quantity of each commodity moved, which routes are activated, and the number of vehicles per route, minimizing total operational cost while meeting priority needs and observing all constraints.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\nDay 0 Demands:\nUnit\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n-----------------------\nU 0        |  11.16 |  36.32\nU 1        |  41.52 |  13.60\nU 2        |  40.40 |  26.61\n\nDay 1 Demands:\nUnit\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n-----------------------\nU 0        |  43.90 |  16.49\nU 1        |  12.66 |  29.05\nU 2        |  39.20 |  14.38\nDay 0 Depot Supplies:\nDepot\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n------------------------\nD 0        |  37.44 |  49.07\nD 1        |  57.31 |  49.50\n\nDay 1 Depot Supplies:\nDepot\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n------------------------\nD 0        |  55.65 |  26.99\nD 1        |  43.57 |  44.74\nTransport Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2\n----------------------------\nD 0        |   1.28 |   3.37 |   4.75\nD 1        |   3.06 |   3.31 |   4.95\nRisk Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2\n----------------------------\nD 0        | 132.54 | 195.62 | 190.13\nD 1        | 134.33 | 174.98 | 122.62\nPenalty Costs per Unit Shortage: [Supply S0: 56.76, Supply S1: 79.83]\nVolume per Supply Unit: [Supply S0: 1.92, Supply S1: 1.66]\nFleet Parameters: Cost 10.0, Capacity 100.0, Total 20",
